Subject: [Vita] Fail closed on Ruby startup and preserve fiber state on allocation failure

Check TLS keys and worker startup before Ruby runs; report worker setup errors
in the parent using the existing interrupt condition. Optional EC lookups are
safe before key setup and on foreign threads. Allocate and root passing values
before acquiring a fiber slot. Let configure measure scalar types and reject
stale ABI caches with target compilation assertions.

